  "findings": [
    "B9-NOTE-DISPLAY: Java builds note Display with escaped-newline expansion before measuring the component. Rust stores the inline text verbatim and note_visual_lines splits physical newlines only. The composite receives one long line instead of two, producing width368/height187 versus Java301/203 in the unstyled reverse control. Identical content in block-form multiline passes. This shared Display dependency is inside the claimed note preferred-dimension invariant and cannot disappear merely because the new envelope equation is otherwise correct. Next repair: Normalize note Display line semantics once before shared measurement and painting, with escaped and block forms as separate regression cases. Do not repair only canvas arithmetic or special-case these labels.",
    "B9-NOTE-ALIGNMENT: The new CENTER margin arithmetic is correct when its input is CENTER, but noteTextAlignment is not consumed: only defaulttextalignment assigns note_text_align. The fresh explicit CENTER single-line case is 9px too narrow with text9px too far left, exactly the lost constructor margin15 versus6; RIGHT preserves the shape but places text7px left. Scoped <style> note Shadowing7 also never reaches the component preferred dimension or filter: Rust has no filter and is7px short in both dimensions in its single-line control. Boolean global shadow's single-line LEFT control passes. Correct equations with missing style inputs do not satisfy the account's styled component claim. Next repair: Resolve the note's effective alignment and numeric shadow through the same style/skinparam inputs used for component paint, then feed those values into preferred dimensions and the complete event envelope. Preserve theme dominance and avoid adding shadow twice.",
    "B9-THEME-ACTIVATION: After removing escaped multiline note text, the cerulean composite's geometry and theme bounds match. Its two activation rectangles still use Rust's hardcoded #181818 stroke rather than the Java merged activation style #2683B9. This was present before the packet and is a shared style dependency, not a newly introduced envelope regression. Next repair: Carry the effective activation line style into activation_bar_segment; retain the exact theme case and keep the bounded note-envelope evidence distinct from whole styled-sequence acceptance.",
    "All source accounts and refinements precede their implementation commits; source audit found no fixture-label matching, golden reads in shipping additions, branch-count ladders, or coordinate-keyed output surgery. The moved generic created-head group unwrapping existed before this packet. Constants and remaining style provenance limitations are recorded in source-audit.json.",
    "Independent1828 CLI replay: before1208 matches/581 valid mismatches/39 invalid; after1232/557/39;24 gains,0 lost passes,0 valid CLI errors/panics/timeouts. Both source/reference and before/after output hashes match archived evidence. Duplicate48 entries retained; frozen955=403 matches/542 mismatches/10 invalid. Nineteen corrected negative rejections are separate from positive matches.",
    "Main library tiers:11181/11251 product and10497/11251 assisted, sequence1411/1411; units567 parser+783 renderer and13 CLI pass. Both main tiers exit101; guards4/6 exit101; changed-file formatting exits0. Initial main-tier invocation failed setup on the empty submodule before rendering; exact pinned golden archive restored and one populated-corpus run performed. All nonzero test exits retained.",
